WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.920
Myth or truth? Stretching before training does not protect you.

2
00:00:03.920 --> 00:00:07.560
And note: I am not talking about warming up, only about stretching.

3
00:00:07.560 --> 00:00:13.000
A study of 26,000 athletes found no reduction in injury risk from it.

4
00:00:13.000 --> 00:00:15.400
And what about jogging a few minutes to warm up?

5
00:00:15.400 --> 00:00:18.080
There is no clear evidence that this alone protects you either.

6
00:00:18.080 --> 00:00:22.200
What does reduce injuries is warming up with strength and balance exercises.

7
00:00:22.200 --> 00:00:25.240
Between 30% and 70% fewer injuries.

8
00:00:25.240 --> 00:00:29.080
So next time, before you start, add strength and balance.

9
00:00:29.080 --> 00:00:33.300
Send this to anyone who thinks stretching or a short jog is enough to avoid injury.

